{"id":"reichlich","lemma":"reichlich","pos":"adv","rank":3648,"glosses":["abundantly, copiously","quite, rather, all too","more than, upwards of"],"ipa":"/ˈʁaɪ̯çlɪç/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6b/De-reichlich.ogg/De-reichlich.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Wir haben reichlich wenig Zeit.","en":"We have precious little time.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"have"},null,{"g":"little, few"},{"g":"time"}]},{"text":"Du hast reichlich Zeit.","en":"You've got plenty of time.","words":[{"g":"you"},{"g":"have","l":"haben"},null,{"g":"time"}]},{"text":"Wir haben reichlich Wasser zur Verfügung.","en":"We have a plentiful supply of water.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"have"},null,{"g":"water"},{"g":"to the"},{"g":"disposal, disposition"}]},{"text":"Du bist reichlich müde, oder?","en":"You're feeling very sleepy, aren't you?","words":[{"g":"you"},{"g":"are","l":"sein"},null,{"g":"tired"},{"g":"or"}]},{"text":"Es gibt reichlich zu essen.","en":"There is plenty of food.","words":[null,null,null,{"g":"to / too"},{"g":"to eat"}],"phrases":[[0,2,"there is, there are"]]}]}